{"profile":{"name":"Chris Moise","ward":"Ward 13, Toronto Centre","bio":"Chris Moise was elected as City Councillor for Ward 13, Toronto Centre on October 24, 2022, winning 48.48% of the vote (10,457 votes). He previously served six years as a Toronto District School Board Trustee (including as vice-chair), worked as an addictions counsellor at St. Michael's Hospital for 22 years and as a police officer in Waterloo, and has run a small business in the St. Lawrence Neighbourhood for over 17 years.","committees":["Board of Health (Chair)","Budget Committee","Civic Appointments Committee","Economic and Community Development Committee","Toronto and East York Community Council (Chair)","Two-Spirit, Lesbian, Gay, Bisexual, Transgender and Queer Advisory Committee (Chair)","Committee of Revision","Board of Directors of TO Live","Board of Governors of Exhibition Place","Canadian National Exhibition Association, Municipal Section and Board of Directors","Association of Municipalities of Ontario, Board of Directors and Executive Committee","Federation of Canadian Municipalities Board of Directors","Mayor's Small Business Champion"],"contact":{"email":"councillor_moise@toronto.ca","phone":"416-392-7904"},"promises":[{"text":"Encourage the construction of all housing types -- multiplexes, high-rises, and public, market, and transitional housing -- to make Toronto a safe space for all.","source":"https://storeys.com/toronto-new-city-councillor-elects/"},{"text":"Address the interconnected nature of the housing, mental health, and addiction crises.","source":"https://storeys.com/toronto-new-city-councillor-elects/"},{"text":"Work with post-secondary institutions to help housing accessibility for students on and around campus.","source":"https://storeys.com/toronto-new-city-councillor-elects/"}]},"lobbying":{"total":489,"term":489,"first":"2022-11-17","last":"2026-10-08","lobbyists":119,"clients":98,"subjects":201,"methods":{"Meetings":258,"Emails":189,"Phone calls":19,"Written":1